@startuml remote-worker-retire
!theme plain
title Lifecycle of a remote worker (revision 2): stop, leave and purge on the donor; suspend, retire and revoke on our side; the identity stays pinned unless revoked

actor "Operator (our side)" as OP
participant "Registry / key keeper" as T
participant "Dispatcher + helper\n(our host)" as D
participant "Bridge (M3) + sshd" as BR
actor "Donor (the machine's owner)" as ADM
participant "curator remote-worker\n(donor; bridge identity)" as C
participant "Privileged helper (donor)" as PH

note over OP, PH
  States: enrolled -> active <-> stopped (donor) | suspended (project) -> retired -> revoked -> purged.
  Stop and revocation marks are persisted BEFORE any process is touched, so a service restart cannot race them.
  Removing an SSH key never substitutes for closing established sessions and killing jobs.
end note

== donor: stop (pause) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker stop
C -> C: persist "stopped"; end the harness identity's processes; keep the bridge service and the keys; audit line
C --> ADM: stopped (run resumes it)

== donor: leave (retire the workplace, keep the identity) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker leave
C -> BR: retire request over the channel (if reachable)
C -> C: close the channel; keep K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh and the configuration
C --> ADM: left; "init --rejoin" with a new invitation returns this identity to a new workplace

== project: suspend / retire / revoke ==
OP -> T: suspend: grants paused
OP -> D: retire workplace
D -> BR: revoke channel authorization; close open sessions
D -> D: kill every job and its descendants (process group / cgroup); verify no process of the workplace UID remains;\nremove the authorized key; archive permitted noncredential artifacts only; release account and egress rules
BR -> BR: next frame or envelope from this worker refused (retired); mailbox kept durable
note right of BR: the donor's connection drops; its bridge reports "retired by project" and pauses
OP -> T: revoke (only on compromise or departure): root-signed revocation of K_sig, K_enc, K_ssh
T -> BR: revocation record: every frame and envelope from these keys refuses from now on;\na return needs a new key through a new enrolment (rotation is a root-authorized record)

== donor: purge (destroy) ==
ADM -> C: curator remote-worker purge --confirm
C -> BR: report purge; ask revocation outcome (if reachable)
alt channel reachable
  BR --> C: revocation outcome (retired | revoked)
else channel unreachable
  C -> C: record "channel unreachable; the project side must revoke separately"
end
C -> C: delete keys, locked config, managed home; audit kept for the donor
C -> PH: remove-worker <label>: both accounts, egress anchor, sandbox profile, daemon unit (journal, rollback)
PH --> C: done
C --> ADM: removed; nothing of the project remains on this machine; revocation outcome printed
@enduml
